-- title:
--   Étale lifting along a nilpotent thickening of an affine base
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a commutative ring and $J \subseteq C$ an ideal that is nilpotent as an element of the multiplicative monoid of ideals of $C$. Let $X$ and $Y_0$ be schemes (in the smallest universe), let $f : X \to \operatorname{Spec} C$ be a morphism, form the fibre product of $f$ with $\operatorname{Spec}(C/J) \to \operatorname{Spec} C$, and let $q_0 : Y_0 \to X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} C} \operatorname{Spec}(C/J)$ be étale. The assertion is that there exist a scheme $Y$, a morphism $q : Y \to X$ which is étale, and a morphism $j : Y_0 \to Y$ such that the square formed by $j$, $q_0$, $q$ and the first projection $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} C} \operatorname{Spec}(C/J) \to X$ is a pullback square (so $Y_0 \cong Y \times_X X_0$ compatibly with $q_0$), and such that the following lifting property holds for affine test schemes: for every commutative ring $B$ with a $C$-algebra structure, every morphism $t : \operatorname{Spec} B \to X$ satisfying $t \circ f = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $C \to B$, and every morphism $s_0 : \operatorname{Spec}(B/JB) \to Y_0$ whose composite with $q_0$ and the first projection to $X$ equals the composite of $\operatorname{Spec}(B/JB) \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ with $t$, there is a unique $s : \operatorname{Spec} B \to Y$ with $s \circ q = t$ and with the restriction of $s$ along $\operatorname{Spec}(B/JB) \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ equal to $j \circ s_0$. Here $JB$ denotes the ideal generated by the image of $J$ in $B$. Note that the lifting clause is quantified over affine $C$-schemes only, and that the compatibility imposed on $s_0$ is stated through the projection to $X$ alone.
--
--   This is the topological invariance of the étale site for a nilpotent thickening of the base, in the form of existence and uniqueness of an étale lift $Y \to X$ of an étale $Y_0 \to X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} C} \operatorname{Spec}(C/J)$ together with unique lifting of affine test points. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where sections over a local ring $S$ with nilpotent ideal $(\pi)$ must be lifted in the analysis of edge charts for fake elliptic curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_etale_isPullback_forall_existsUnique_comp_eq_of_isNilpotent.lean

